.Sh NAME
.Nm ghg
.Nd Play games on heaphones with volume buttons. Games can be programmed with JSON instructions.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op path to game directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
command starts a game made for heaphones with volume buttons.
.Pp
It plays audio and changes variables based off of input given
through input buttons.
.Pp
The volume keys are setup such that
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "xxxx" -compact -offset indent
.It +
answers yes to a question
.It -
answers no to a question
.El
.Pp
.Sh FILES
The filesystem structure of a generalized headphone game directory is as follows:

NameOfGame
.Bl -tag -width "xxxxxxxxxxxxx" -compact -offset indent
.It currency.txt
The name of the currency in the game.
.It init.json
The entry point for the game.
.It stage
The code for stages.
Each stage is named [number].json.
.It backpack.json
Generated while the game is being played. Contains money and backpack fields.
.It stage.txt
Contains which stage the user is on. Generated by setstage (documented below).
.El
